      "writtenOn": "2021-07-14T15:10:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "To my knowledge Soong consistently uses strings with separators in them for identifiers of different sorts: visibility references, fully qualified module names, :file references, paths, etc. I don\u0027t think this is any different - for these use cases strings with some syntax in them is way more convenient than completely structured types.\n\nBut if you see some aspect here that I don\u0027t then I shan\u0027t block it. It still gets the job done.",
